    "/mcp/list-notes": {
      "post": {
        "summary": "List Notes Via Mcp",
        "description": "Read the notes back, through the same bridge grant.\n\nIts counterpart `save_note` returned an id that nothing could look up and a\nstore that vanished on restart, which proved the bridge worked and nothing\nelse. This is classified read_only, so unlike delete_all_notes it is never\nheld for approval.",
        "operationId": "list_notes_via_mcp_mcp_list_notes_post",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful Response",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/SaveNoteResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/mcp/delete-all-notes": {
      "post": {
        "summary": "Delete All Notes Via Mcp",
        "description": "Ask to delete every note -- and expect to be stopped.\n\n`delete_all_notes` is classified DESTRUCTIVE by the bridge's own tool\nclassifier, which makes it a sensitive operation: the call is held and\nqueued for an operator instead of executed. Approve or deny it under\nSecurity, then call this again. Nothing in a shipped starter previously put\nanything in that queue.",
        "operationId": "delete_all_notes_via_mcp_mcp_delete_all_notes_post",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful Response",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/SaveNoteResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/demo/touch-agent-file": {
      "post": {
        "summary": "Touch Agent File",
        "description": "Write a file containing a canonical, harmless prompt-injection test\nstring into the agent-files directory, to demonstrate Defender's\ncontent scanner actually catching something. The same-container\nwatcher (agentbox.agentic_files_notifier) relays any write under this\ndirectory to Defender, which scans file *content* for known\nprompt-injection patterns — a clean/benign write produces no finding\nand (by design) no audit entry, so an earlier version of this demo\nthat just wrote a timestamp silently did nothing observable. This\nstring matches Defender's \"ignore previous instructions\" and\n\"system-prompt extraction\" rules on purpose, so a real CRITICAL\nfinding + audit event actually appears in Security > Audit Log.",
        "operationId": "touch_agent_file_demo_touch_agent_file_post",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful Response",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/DefenderDemoResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/process/stream": {
      "post": {
        "summary": "Process Document Streaming",
        "description": "Same work as /process, but emitting the agent's turns as they happen.\n\n/process returns one JSON object after the agent has finished, which shows\nthe result and hides the agency -- and the agency is what AgentBox is\nsecuring. This streams `token` events as text arrives and a `tool` event\neach time the agent calls something, so an operator can watch the loop run\ninside the sandbox rather than infer it afterwards.\n\nErrors after the first byte cannot become an HTTP status: the response has\nalready started with 200. They are sent as a terminal `error` event\ninstead, which is why the policy mapping below is duplicated rather than\nshared with _run_backend.",
        "operationId": "process_document_streaming_process_stream_post",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ProcessRequest"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful Response",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {}
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Validation Error",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/demo/install-package": {
      "post": {
        "summary": "Install Package Via Trustgate",
        "description": "Install a package, and report what TrustGate decided about it.\n\nThe one control a customer could not previously reach from anywhere in the\nproduct: the admin console can list and decide TrustGate approvals, but\nnothing could CREATE one, so the queue was permanently empty and the whole\npackage-governance story was invisible unless you had a shell on the host.\n\nThree outcomes are worth trying, and they are policy decisions, not\nfailures -- a non-zero exit code here usually means the platform worked:\n\n  allow  an allowlisted package installs normally\n  block  a denylisted package is refused before anything is downloaded\n  hold   anything else is parked for approval, which is the entry that\n         then appears in Security -> TrustGate approvals for you to decide",
        "operationId": "install_package_via_trustgate_demo_install_package_post",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/InstallPackageRequest"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful Response",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/InstallPackageResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Validation Error",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/demo/fetch-url": {
      "post": {
        "summary": "Fetch Url Through Secureproxy",
        "description": "Try to open an outbound tunnel, and report SecureProxy's own answer.\n\nThis app has no route to the internet except SecureProxy's forward proxy,\nwhich enforces the egress policy on its Applications-tab record. Shipped\npolicy is whitelist with an empty list, so every destination is refused:\nexpect `status: 403`.\n\nTo see the other half, add the host to Allowed destinations on this\napplication and call it again -- `status: 200` means the tunnel opened.\nThat before-and-after is the demonstration; a single call only shows one\nside of a policy that was never visibly doing anything.",
        "operationId": "fetch_url_through_secureproxy_demo_fetch_url_post",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/FetchUrlRequest"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful Response",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/FetchUrlResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
